  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}).\n\nCONJUGATION: サ{変|へん}{動詞|どうし} (irregular する verb): {臆|おく}しない, {臆|おく}します, {臆|おく}して.\n\nNUANCE: {臆|おく}する is a literary/formal word implying cowardice or losing nerve. It's often used in negative constructions ({臆|おく}せず, {臆|おく}することなく) to describe courage or determination.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {臆|おく}することなく (without flinching)\n- {臆|おく}せずに (unflinchingly)\n- ～に{臆|おく}する (to be daunted by ~)\n\nRELATED ADJECTIVE: {臆病|おくびょう} (cowardly, timid)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {物怖|ものお}じする (to be shy/timid)\n- {気後|きおく}れする (to feel intimidated)\n- {怯|ひる}む (to flinch, cower)\n- {尻込|しりご}みする (to shrink back)",
